WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.234
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book three.

2
00:00:05.534 --> 00:00:08.851
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.151 --> 00:00:15.321
Unit ten: Digital Communication. Today you will talk about online rules with must and should.

4
00:00:15.621 --> 00:00:18.192
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.133 --> 00:00:22.494
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:23.350 --> 00:00:24.281
Etiquette.

7
00:00:25.283 --> 00:00:27.527
Etiquette means rules of polite behaviour.

8
00:00:28.117 --> 00:00:30.279
Table etiquette is important at dinner.

9
00:00:30.883 --> 00:00:33.083
Your turn. Say: Etiquette.

10
00:00:35.933 --> 00:00:36.888
Etiquette.

11
00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:38.616
Emoji.

12
00:00:39.617 --> 00:00:42.742
Emoji means a small picture used in messages.

13
00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:45.837
A smile emoji makes a message friendly.

14
00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:48.859
Your turn. Say: Emoji.

15
00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:52.689
Emoji.

16
00:00:53.450 --> 00:00:54.172
Tone.

17
00:00:55.183 --> 00:00:57.903
Tone means the feeling or attitude in your words.

18
00:00:58.517 --> 00:01:00.795
Your tone can sound rude in a text.

19
00:01:01.383 --> 00:01:03.548
Your turn. Say: Tone.

20
00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:07.157
Tone.

21
00:01:07.917 --> 00:01:09.243
Miscommunication.

22
00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:14.258
Miscommunication means when people don't understand each other correctly.

23
00:01:14.850 --> 00:01:17.476
A short reply caused a miscommunication.

24
00:01:18.083 --> 00:01:20.829
Your turn. Say: Miscommunication.

25
00:01:23.667 --> 00:01:25.074
Miscommunication.

26
00:01:25.817 --> 00:01:27.143
Instant messaging.

27
00:01:28.150 --> 00:01:31.020
Instant messaging means sending quick messages online.

28
00:01:31.617 --> 00:01:33.965
We use instant messaging for group work.

29
00:01:34.550 --> 00:01:37.690
Your turn. Say: Instant messaging.

30
00:01:40.533 --> 00:01:41.906
Instant messaging.

31
00:01:42.650 --> 00:01:43.767
Video call.

32
00:01:44.783 --> 00:01:47.909
Video call means talking to someone online with a camera.

33
00:01:48.517 --> 00:01:51.062
I had a video call with my cousin in Korea.

34
00:01:51.650 --> 00:01:54.256
Your turn. Say: Video call.

35
00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:58.182
Video call.

36
00:01:58.917 --> 00:02:00.011
Netiquette.

37
00:02:01.017 --> 00:02:03.899
Netiquette means polite rules for behaving online.

38
00:02:04.483 --> 00:02:06.982
Good netiquette means no all-caps shouting.

39
00:02:07.583 --> 00:02:10.247
Your turn. Say: Netiquette.

40
00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:14.171
Netiquette.

41
00:02:14.917 --> 00:02:15.732
Clarity.

42
00:02:16.717 --> 00:02:19.622
Clarity means being clear and easy to understand.

43
00:02:20.217 --> 00:02:22.216
Clarity is important in emails.

44
00:02:22.817 --> 00:02:25.446
Your turn. Say: Clarity.

45
00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:29.255
Clarity.

46
00:02:30.017 --> 00:02:31.134
Context.

47
00:02:32.150 --> 00:02:35.415
Context means the situation that helps explain meaning.

48
00:02:36.017 --> 00:02:39.224
Without context, a joke can seem rude.

49
00:02:39.817 --> 00:02:42.492
Your turn. Say: Context.

50
00:02:45.333 --> 00:02:46.311
Context.

51
00:02:47.050 --> 00:02:48.515
Respond promptly.

52
00:02:49.517 --> 00:02:52.073
Respond promptly means to answer quickly.

53
00:02:52.683 --> 00:02:54.845
Please respond promptly to your teacher.

54
00:02:55.450 --> 00:02:58.288
Your turn. Say: Respond promptly.

55
00:03:01.133 --> 00:03:02.610
Respond promptly.

56
00:03:03.350 --> 00:03:04.374
Professional.

57
00:03:05.383 --> 00:03:08.985
Professional means suitable for work or formal situations.

58
00:03:09.583 --> 00:03:12.175
Use a professional tone with teachers.

59
00:03:12.783 --> 00:03:15.494
Your turn. Say: Professional.

60
00:03:18.333 --> 00:03:19.288
Professional.

61
00:03:20.050 --> 00:03:20.970
Casual.

62
00:03:21.983 --> 00:03:24.157
Casual means relaxed and informal.

63
00:03:24.750 --> 00:03:27.040
With friends, a casual tone is fine.

64
00:03:27.650 --> 00:03:30.151
Your turn. Say: Casual.

65
00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:33.920
Casual.

66
00:03:34.733 --> 00:03:38.918
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:39.783 --> 00:03:43.829
Visal, a classmate was upset by your message. What happened?

68
00:03:44.917 --> 00:03:48.927
I wrote 'OK.' Maybe the tone sounded rude.

69
00:03:50.017 --> 00:03:54.132
That's a miscommunication. You should add context or an emoji.

70
00:03:55.217 --> 00:03:56.694
Are there other rules?

71
00:03:57.783 --> 00:04:01.420
You must respond politely, and you should be clear in messages.

72
00:04:02.517 --> 00:04:06.388
Got it. Casual with friends, professional with teachers!

73
00:04:07.533 --> 00:04:09.324
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:10.183 --> 00:04:13.297
Grammar focus: Modal verbs of obligation.

75
00:04:13.597 --> 00:04:14.784
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:15.483 --> 00:04:17.297
You must respond politely.

77
00:04:18.183 --> 00:04:20.102
You should be clear in messages.

78
00:04:21.017 --> 00:04:23.365
You mustn't share private screenshots.

79
00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:29.265
'Must' is a strong rule. 'Should' is advice. Both are followed by the base verb.

80
00:04:30.017 --> 00:04:33.737
Be careful! Don't say: You must to respond politely.

81
00:04:35.700 --> 00:04:38.199
Say: You must respond politely.

82
00:04:38.499 --> 00:04:40.080
Don't use 'to' after 'must'.

83
00:04:40.867 --> 00:04:43.298
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:45.519
Netiquette Matters.

85
00:04:45.819 --> 00:04:49.154
Good digital etiquette means responding promptly and being clear.

86
00:04:50.167 --> 00:04:52.700
Tone is easy to misread in instant messaging.

87
00:04:53.700 --> 00:04:56.559
You should add context to avoid miscommunication.

88
00:04:57.567 --> 00:05:00.948
On a video call, you must be on time and listen.

89
00:05:01.933 --> 00:05:05.918
Use a casual tone with friends and a professional tone with teachers.

90
00:05:07.033 --> 00:05:10.687
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:05:11.550 --> 00:05:14.307
You blank respond politely. It's a rule.

92
00:05:14.607 --> 00:05:17.726
A, must. B, could. C, might.

93
00:05:21.267 --> 00:05:22.988
The answer is A: must.

94
00:05:24.150 --> 00:05:26.672
Polite rules for behaving online are blank.

95
00:05:26.972 --> 00:05:31.032
A, netiquette. B, emoji. C, context.

96
00:05:34.567 --> 00:05:36.671
The answer is A: netiquette.

97
00:05:37.817 --> 00:05:39.979
Relaxed and informal is blank.

98
00:05:40.279 --> 00:05:43.897
A, casual. B, professional. C, prompt.

99
00:05:47.433 --> 00:05:49.700
The answer is A: casual.

100
00:05:50.900 --> 00:05:54.005
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:05:54.850 --> 00:05:57.268
What rules of digital etiquette do you follow?

102
00:06:06.083 --> 00:06:07.537
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:06:07.837 --> 00:06:17.200
I always respond promptly to my teacher, and I use a professional tone. With friends, I'm casual, but I must never send unkind messages.

104
00:06:17.500 --> 00:06:19.233
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:20.117 --> 00:06:24.882
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and modal verbs of obligation.

106
00:06:25.182 --> 00:06:28.612
Today's value is respect. Thank the people who help us.

107
00:06:28.912 --> 00:06:31.565
See you in Unit eleven. Goodbye!

108
00:06:31.865 --> 00:06:34.888
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

